# Aiken contracts

## Layout

```
validators/   # spend/mint validators — thin orchestration
lib/          # pure types, math (waterfall, shares), shared checks
```

- One **primary purpose** per validator module (e.g. vault spend, credit spend, share mint, whitelist mint).
- Shared logic lives in `lib/`; validators wire **inputs, outputs, datums, redeemers, and signatures**.

## Validator discipline

- **Exhaustive redeemers:** every variant handled; unknown paths fail.
- **Preserve value:** when continuing a script UTxO, output value must include at least the locked assets the datum expects (no accidental drain except via defined redeemers).
- **Validity interval:** use `validity_range` when time bounds matter (loan schedule, attestation freshness if modeled on-chain).
- **Constants** (asset names, max fee bps caps, tranche tags): single module in `lib/` (e.g. `lib/constants.ak`), not magic literals scattered in validators.

## Forbidden in MVP

```aiken
// BAD — no upgrade path in phase 1
Upgrade { new_script_hash: Hash<Script> }

// BAD — custodial “admin withdraw arbitrary value” without loan/vault rules
AdminDrain
```

- No proxy indirection validator whose only job is swapping script hashes.
- Curator power is limited to **configured** actions (origination, parameter updates in datum, whitelist mint/burn), each enforced by explicit checks.

## Transactions

- Document expected **input/output graph** in module doc comments for each redeemer (which UTxOs must appear, which signatures).
- Prefer reading **datum from the spent output** and checking **output datum continuity** on the same script address.

## Before merge

- Run `aiken check` (and `aiken build` when CI exists). Fix all compiler warnings in touched files.
